two animals killed at a popular tourist  spot on fossil ridge in charleston in  the red rock conservation area so park  rangers with the bureau of land  management are trying to find out who's  responsible mary jane bellissa takes us  to cowboy trail rides and shares the  owner's plea tonight  when you hear innocent animals being  shot you know it i think you'd have to  be a sick individual for it to not  bother you a little bit michael flood  ranch manager of cowboy trail rides is  worried about the rest of his animals  after a series of attacks on his horses  and mules the first incident started  four weeks ago when he suspected someone  unlocked the gate and let all the horses  out after that we had a three-year-old  horse in really good health  that we had rode the day before been  with he ended up dead in the pin the  next morning we can't confirm that he  was shot blood says he's never  experienced anything like this during  his 26 years of operation  the next weekend we had  more horses turned out  and  that was a little strange and this last  saturday we had one of our mules in the  pen and she was shot in the head and  killed and we confirmed that she was  shot in the head cowboy trail rides is  on blm land blm rangers will be  investigating this case along with  assistance from the las vegas metro  police department in the meantime mike  floyd is asking the community for help  if they have any information leading to  the guy or you know have heard somebody  saying you know something about cowboy  trail rides and not liking horses we'd  love to have information given to the  rangers or the blm or anyone that you  know is willing to help we would love  all the help we can get reporting in red  rock mary jane balleza live local now  so you're asked to call metro crime  stoppers tip line that number is  702-385-5555  if you have any information and remember  that you can remain anonymous
 

